---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Reveal from "@/components/atoms/Reveal.astro";
import LabCard from "@/components/molecules/LabCard.astro";
import WorkingLoopMap from "@/components/molecules/WorkingLoopMap.astro";
import { getShowcaseLabProjects } from "@/data/lab";

const projects = getShowcaseLabProjects();
const stats = [
  { value: String(projects.length).padStart(2, "0"), label: "Projects in this shortlist" },
  { value: "Inspect → test", label: "What they share" },
  { value: "Figma ↔ code", label: "Where I prototype" },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Lab" description="Six projects for reviewing AI output, mapping agent behaviour, designing chat patterns, and connecting Figma with code.">
  <div class="page container">
    <Reveal>
      <h1 class="page-header__title">Lab</h1>
    </Reveal>

    <div class="spacer-md"></div>

    <Reveal class="lab-intro">
      <p>I can make the first version of an AI prototype quickly. Checking whether it behaves as intended takes longer. These projects explore how to describe behaviour, compare one change, review a recorded flow, and show enough context for someone else to challenge the result.</p>
      <p>I chose six projects for this page. Some work end to end; others test one part of a tool I wish existed. I pair-programmed most of them with Claude Code. I set the problem, made the product decisions, and checked the details.</p>
    </Reveal>

    <Reveal>
      <div class="lab-stat-row">
        {stats.map((s) => (
          <div>
            <p class="lab-stat__value">{s.value}</p>
            <p class="lab-stat__label">{s.label}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </Reveal>

    <Reveal class="lab-working-loop">
      <WorkingLoopMap />
    </Reveal>

    <section class="lab-category">
      <Reveal class="lab-category__head">
        <h2 class="section-label">Selected projects</h2>
        <span class="lab-category__count">{String(projects.length).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
      </Reveal>
      <div class="lab-grid">
        {projects.map((project, i) => (
          <Reveal delay={i * 60}>
            <LabCard project={project} />
          </Reveal>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <Reveal class="lab-archive-note">
      <p>There are also smaller utilities, marketing sites, and unfinished experiments. I left them out here to keep the page focused on the six projects above.</p>
    </Reveal>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
